@startuml seq_sta_poweron_valid_app
title SC-STA-01 - Power-on with a valid application, no tester

participant "Plant model" as Plant
box "TCU"
participant "PBL" as PBL
participant "Application" as App
end box
participant "Red LED\n(TCU board)" as LED

note over Plant, LED
Covers: SYS-BOOT-001, SYS-BOOT-011, SYS-BOOT-013, SYS-BOOT-008, SYS-ACT-004, SYS-STA-001,
SYS-SEL-001, SYS-COM-002, SYS-COM-004, SYS-TIM-001, SYS-FLT-001, SYS-FLT-002, SYS-HMI-001,
SIM-PLT-001, SIM-PLT-004
CAN frames pass can0 / slcand / gateway transparently (DC-05, SIM-GW-001), see SC-STA-04.
end note

== t0: reset (power-on) ==

loop every 10 ms, from before the reset and during the whole scenario (SIM-PLT-001)
  Plant -> PBL : SIM_Driver (0x100), SIM_Speed (0x101), SIM_Analog (0x102), AliveCtr +1 per frame
  note right: the PBL does not use plant signals (SYS-BOOT-011 note)
end

PBL -> PBL : application check (SYS-BOOT-001, reprogramming section 9 row 1):\nheader magic 0x41544178, header_crc32, hw_id 0x0947_0001,\nmin_pbl_version <= PBL version, image CRC32 -> valid
note right of PBL: completes without a processor fault\nalso for an erased or partial area (SYS-BOOT-013)
PBL -> PBL : boot window: listen for 10 02 on 0x7E1 (SYS-BOOT-011)
... 50 ms, no 10 02 received ...
PBL -> PBL : de-initialize CAN and clocks, set the vector table\n(reprogramming section 9 row 3)
PBL -> App : jump to the application
note over PBL: no TCU_Actuators / TCU_Status from the PBL (SYS-BOOT-008)

== Init: from reset until control is active ==

note over App
no TCU_Actuators (SYS-ACT-004) and no TCU_Status (SYS-COM-004 note)
selector position = N until the first position is accepted (SYS-SEL-001)
substitute values (can_matrix section 6) until the first reception of each message;
reception timeouts (30 ms) are monitored from the application start (SYS-COM-002)
end note

Plant -> Plant : TCU_Actuators not received for 50 ms (t0 + 50 ms):\nhydraulic default SS_A = SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %, RLS = OFF,\nSLS = OFF, FaultLamp = OFF (SIM-PLT-004)
note right of Plant: 3rd gear in D, maximum line pressure,\nreverse locked out, selector locked in P\n(system_context section 4 item 3)

alt plant model running
  Plant -> App : SIM_Driver: Selector = 0 (P), Brake, Throttle; SIM_Speed; SIM_Analog
  App -> App : first reception replaces the substitute values (SYS-COM-002)
  ... Selector = 0 (P) received unchanged for 50 ms ...
  App -> App : P accepted (SYS-SEL-001); control active, mode Normal
  App -> Plant : TCU_Actuators (0x200): SS_A = ON, SS_B = ON (1st prepared, SYS-SEL-005),\nPCS_Duty from the table (SYS-ACT-002), RLS = OFF, SLS per SYS-SEL-003, FaultLamp = OFF
else no message of the plant model received
  ... 30 ms after the application start ...
  App -> App : communication faults SIM_Driver, SIM_Speed, SIM_Analog\n(FaultBits 7, 8, 9) (SYS-COM-002) -> enter limp-home (SYS-FLT-002)
  App -> App : control active with the limp-home outputs (SYS-STA-001 note)
  App -> Plant : TCU_Actuators (0x200): SS_A = OFF, SS_B = OFF, PCS_Duty = 0 %,\nFaultLamp = ON, RLS = OFF, SLS = OFF (SYS-FLT-001)
  App -> LED : ON (SYS-HMI-001)
end
note over PBL, App: control active <= 500 ms after t0, including the PBL check (SYS-STA-001)

== control active ==

loop every 10 ms (+/- 1 ms) (SYS-TIM-001, SYS-COM-004)
  Plant -> App : SIM_Driver, SIM_Speed, SIM_Analog
  App -> App : sensor inputs, selector logic, shift control,\nactuator commands, fault detection (SYS-TIM-001)
  App -> Plant : TCU_Actuators (0x200)
end
loop every 100 ms (+/- 1 ms) (SYS-TIM-001, SYS-COM-004)
  App -> Plant : TCU_Status (0x201): GearActual, GearTarget, Mode,\nSelectorState, VehicleSpeed, FaultBits, OilTemp
end
Plant -> Plant : uses TCU_Actuators again (SIM-PLT-004 no longer active)
@enduml
